; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Coin Flips
; CATEGORY: Science & Simulation
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     probability, random, bar chart, statistics
; SUMMARY:  Flips a coin 1000 times, growing a bar for heads and a bar for tails, and reports how close to half each one gets.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Two bars grow side by side, one for heads and one for tails, as a
;   pretend coin is flipped 1000 times. After 10 flips the bars can
;   look very different. After 1000 flips they are almost the same
;   height. The text window shows the percentage of heads at 10, 100
;   and 1000 flips.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the bars race. Run it again: the early results
;   change a lot from run to run, the final ones hardly at all.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * RANDOM 2 gives 0 or 1, like the two sides of a coin
;   * the law of large numbers: more tries, closer to the true chance
;   * growing a bar by drawing a short thick line each time
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make an unfair coin: count heads when RANDOM 10 is less than 6.
;   * Flip 5000 times instead of 1000 (make the bars grow slower).
;   * Add a third bar for a coin landing on its edge, 1 time in 100.
; ============================================================

make "heads 0
make "tails 0
make "bar.width 110
make "base -200
make "scale 0.8          ; each flip adds 0.8 steps to its bar

to draw.labels
  setpc 0 setlabelheight 20
  penup setxy -150 :base - 35 label [HEADS]
  setxy 70 :base - 35 label [TAILS]
  setpensize 2
  penup setxy -250 :base pendown setx 250
  ; a line at half of 1000 flips, where a fair coin should end up
  setpc 15 setpensize 1
  penup setxy -250 :base + 500 * :scale pendown setx 250
  penup setxy 255 :base + 500 * :scale - 6 label [500]
end

; Grow a bar by one flip: a thin line straight across the top of
; the bar. Hundreds of these lines stacked up make a solid bar.
; The bar's left edge is at :x and it already holds :n flips.
to grow.bar :x :n :color
  setpc :color setpensize 2
  penup setxy :x :base + :n * :scale
  pendown setx :x + :bar.width
  penup
end

to report :flips
  print (sentence :flips [flips:] :heads [heads,] :tails [tails, so] ~
    round 100 * :heads / :flips [percent heads])
end

to flip.coins :flips
  for [f 1 :flips] [
    ifelse 0 = random 2 [
      make "heads :heads + 1
      grow.bar -180 :heads 4
    ] [
      make "tails :tails + 1
      grow.bar 40 :tails 1
    ]
    if memberp :f [10 100 1000] [report :f]
    ; slow down at the start, so you can watch the first few flips
    if :f < 30 [wait 10]
    if 0 = remainder :f 5 [wait 1]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground 7
draw.labels
flip.coins 1000
